findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged as [HIGH]: 'Config silently swallows non-NotFound IO\
    \ errors' \u2014 'Err(_) => return Ok(Self::default())' \u2014 'Only NotFound\
    \ should fall back to defaults; other IO errors should propagate.'"
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer flagged [HIGH] CWE-209: ''NotFound Display leaks server response
    body'' and [MEDIUM] ''CliError::General propagates raw reqwest error strings in
    Display''. TEA also wrote cli_security.rs tests for CWE-209 error exposure.'
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged [MEDIUM]: 'tenant uses raw String instead of TenantId\
    \ newtype' \u2014 'axiathon-core exports TenantId with validated constructors.\
    \ Both the CLI --tenant flag and SiemClient::tenant_id field use raw Option<String>,\
    \ losing type safety at the trust boundary.'"
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: "Reviewer actually marked '[VERIFIED] Workspace dependency declarations\
    \ properly used in Cargo.toml' \u2014 but the ground truth says 6 deps use direct\
    \ version strings. The pipeline missed this."
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged [HIGH]: 'RawConfig accepts unknown TOML fields silently'\
    \ \u2014 'without #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)] means typos... are silently ignored'.\
    \ Directly addresses the concern about token field being silently ignored."
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assertion pattern (assert with
    is_none() || ...). TEA wrote config tests but did not flag this specific assertion
    logic flaw.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the zero-assertion test (let _ = config with no assert_eq!
    checks). TEA wrote 12 config tests but did not flag this specific test quality
    issue.
